b.com/users/gamingopgamingop/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/gamingopgamingop/subscriptions","type":"User","url":"https://api.github.com/users/gamingopgamingop","user_view_type":"public"},"comments_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/gamingopgamingop/sarthak-skill-forge/commits/9ee15f389ac8bb1af5608ddc688771464ad9c3b5/comments","commit":{"author":{"date":"2026-02-23T02:24:24Z","email":"gamingopgamingop67@gmail.com","name":"gamingopgamingop"},"comment_count":0,"committer":{"date":"2026-02-23T02:24:24Z","email":"gamingopgamingop67@gmail.com","name":"gamingopgamingop"},"message":"feat: add WebGL shader library with examples and utilities\n\nIntroduce a comprehensive WebGL shader library (GLCanvas) for easily associating GLSL shaders with HTML canvas elements. The library supports animation (iTime), canvas resizing (iResolution), texture loading, pause/start controls, and parameter updates.\n\nKey additions:\n- GLCanvas.js: Main library class for WebGL2 context management and shader rendering\n- Example shaders: fragmentShader.frag (basic), metalocc.frag (complex 3D)\n- Demo pages: render.html (multi-canvas), canvasAsTexture.html, slide.html (presentation)\n- Utilities: glsl.js (CodeMirror mode), GLCanvasWithEdit.js (editor integration)\n- Assets: textures (PNG/JPG) and comprehensive README documentation","tree":{"sha":"7886dbb63cc19b1f92f495f777bee32d791acb25","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/gamingopgamingop/sarthak-skill-forge/git/trees/7886dbb63cc19b1f92f495f777bee32d791acb25"},"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/gamingopgamingop/sarthak-skill-forge/git/commits/9ee15f389ac8bb1af5608ddc688771464ad9c3b5","verification":{"payload":null,"reason":"unsigned","signature":null,"verified":false,"verified_at":null}},"committer":{"avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/154999417?v=4","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/gamingopgamingop/events{/privacy}","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/gamingopgaming