"TESTPERSONAL","node_id":"MDQ6VXNlcjY2NjQ1ODg=","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/TESTPERSONAL/orgs","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/TESTPERSONAL/received_events","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/TESTPERSONAL/repos","site_admin":false,"starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/TESTPERSONAL/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/TESTPERSONAL/subscriptions","type":"User","url":"https://api.github.com/users/TESTPERSONAL","user_view_type":"public"},"comments_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/Hive-Academy/ptah-extension/commits/461877740c9bd18ab2c420d30230da78cf857d6b/comments","commit":{"author":{"date":"2026-10-07T02:17:58Z","email":"test@test.com","name":"Test"},"comment_count":0,"committer":{"date":"2026-10-07T02:17:58Z","email":"test@test.com","name":"Test"},"message":"fix(memory-curator): catch background curate rejections in trigger callbacks\n\nSonarCloud failed the reliability gate on four floating promises\n(typescript:S9383) in the trigger service. Event callbacks stay\nsynchronous so the SDK event path is not delayed; each background pass\nnow goes through dispatchEpisodeCurate, which logs a rejection instead of\nleaving it unhandled. Also uses an optional chain in the rate-limit\nwindow check (S6582). The two cognitive-complexity smells are deferred\nto avoid changing boot-scan behaviour in this PR.\n\nCo-Authored-By: Claude Opus 5.5 <noreply@anthropic.com>","tree":{"sha":"89433de6e425badedf6ba072262518cd56a75f21","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/Hive-Academy/ptah-extension/git/trees/89433de6e425badedf6ba072262518cd56a75f21"},"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/Hive-Academy/ptah-extension/git/commits/461877740c9bd18ab2c420d30230da78cf857d6b","verification":{"payload":null,"reason":"unsigned","signature":null,"verified":false,"verified_at":null}},"committer":{"avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/6664588?v=4","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/TESTPERS