ithub.com/users/TESTPERSONAL/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/TESTPERSONAL/subscriptions","type":"User","url":"https://api.github.com/users/TESTPERSONAL","user_view_type":"public"},"comments_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/Hive-Academy/ptah-extension/commits/087f50e2677be4499204e5a99de2bc2616750244/comments","commit":{"author":{"date":"2026-10-06T13:50:53Z","email":"test@test.com","name":"Test"},"comment_count":0,"committer":{"date":"2026-10-06T13:50:53Z","email":"test@test.com","name":"Test"},"message":"feat(git-ui): discard all changes and read-only worktree review\n\nDiscard all: the CHANGES header gets a discard button behind a confirm\ndialog. It sends git:discard with worktreeOnly, which never touches the\nindex (staged renames survive), skips conflicted files and runs git in\npath batches that stay under the Windows command-line limit.\n\nWorktree review: a change-set card from a turn that ran in another git\nworktree used to show the active workspace''s files. The Changes tab now\nreads that worktree''s status and diffs in a read-only scope, with a bar\nto go back or open it as a workspace. git:info and git:diffFile accept\na root only if it is a listed, existing, non-prunable worktree that\nshares the open folder''s git common dir; worktree file reads refuse\npaths that resolve outside the root. Write methods still accept only\nopen folders.\n\nCo-Authored-By: Claude Opus 5.5 <noreply@anthropic.com>","tree":{"sha":"ad066b8cea19ee193d3f72f9161462aea97002f8","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/Hive-Academy/ptah-extension/git/trees/ad066b8cea19ee193d3f72f9161462aea97002f8"},"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/Hive-Academy/ptah-extension/git/commits/087f50e2677be4499204e5a99de2bc2616750244","verification":{"payload":null,"reason":"unsigned","signature":null,"verified":false,"verified_at":null}},"committer":{"avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/6664588?v=4","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/TE