ttps://api.github.com/users/TESTPERSONAL/received_events","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/TESTPERSONAL/repos","site_admin":false,"starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/TESTPERSONAL/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/TESTPERSONAL/subscriptions","type":"User","url":"https://api.github.com/users/TESTPERSONAL","user_view_type":"public"},"comments_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/Hive-Academy/ptah-extension/commits/3c5a1b730754f21d48da3d5fd67dcc10e3bd4125/comments","commit":{"author":{"date":"2026-10-06T01:53:00Z","email":"test@test.com","name":"Test"},"comment_count":0,"committer":{"date":"2026-10-06T01:53:00Z","email":"test@test.com","name":"Test"},"message":"refactor(rpc-handlers): split AuthRpcHandlers into focused collaborators\n\nauth-rpc.handlers.ts had grown to 1,875 lines that mixed every auth:* RPC\nmethod with status caching, probe orchestration, device-code broadcast,\nscope handling and tier auto-mapping. Each responsibility now lives in its\nown file under handlers/auth/, and AuthRpcHandlers is a thin composition\nclass that builds them and delegates.\n\nPure move: the constructor (parameters, types, @inject tokens), METHODS,\nregister() order, public invalidateAuthStatusCache(), RPC names, responses,\nerror text, logging and Sentry errorSource strings are unchanged. No new DI\ntokens, so host registration is untouched. No spec file was edited.\n\nCo-Authored-By: Claude Opus 5.5 <noreply@anthropic.com>","tree":{"sha":"e7347ef35c815cd75d561398277a3fde6bb8e2e7","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/Hive-Academy/ptah-extension/git/trees/e7347ef35c815cd75d561398277a3fde6bb8e2e7"},"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/Hive-Academy/ptah-extension/git/commits/3c5a1b730754f21d48da3d5fd67dcc10e3bd4125","verification":{"payload":null,"reason":"unsigned","signature":null,"verified":false,"verified_at":null}},"committer":{"avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/6664588?v=4","events_url":"https://api.gith