64588,"login":"TESTPERSONAL","node_id":"MDQ6VXNlcjY2NjQ1ODg=","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/TESTPERSONAL/orgs","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/TESTPERSONAL/received_events","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/TESTPERSONAL/repos","site_admin":false,"starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/TESTPERSONAL/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/TESTPERSONAL/subscriptions","type":"User","url":"https://api.github.com/users/TESTPERSONAL","user_view_type":"public"},"comments_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/Hive-Academy/ptah-extension/commits/578beaf075312d933268aaa4e19caec2c6f90de9/comments","commit":{"author":{"date":"2026-10-06T00:06:36Z","email":"test@test.com","name":"Test"},"comment_count":0,"committer":{"date":"2026-10-06T00:06:36Z","email":"test@test.com","name":"Test"},"message":"fix(cli-agent-runtime): stop false opencode exit-1 failures and add queued messaging\n\nopencode 2.x exits 1 whenever any step failed, even after a retry\nsucceeded, so lanes that finished their work were reported as failed with\nonly \"opencode CLI exited with code 1\". The adapter also read only the 1.x\nerror shape, hiding the real cause.\n\n- Parse both the 1.x and 2.x error event shapes and surface the message.\n- Treat a non-zero exit as success when a final step_finish (reason stop)\n  follows the last error; emit an info line naming the recovered error.\n- Add continue() via `opencode run --session <id>` with the same flags,\n  MCP env and binary; capabilities() now reports continuation (queue).\n- getPid() returns a PID only while a turn''s child is live, so stop/release\n  can no longer tree-kill a reused PID; getSessionId() falls back to the\n  resume id.\n- Update the agent-lanes skill text that said opencode has no messaging.\n\nRefs TASK_2026_591_fff5\n\nCo-Authored-By: Claude Opus 5.5 <noreply@anthropic.com>","tree":{"sha":"466bbeee761ce282edb2361ad5de1d9e9d85febf","url":"https://api.github.c