XNlcjY2NjQ1ODg=","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/TESTPERSONAL/orgs","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/TESTPERSONAL/received_events","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/TESTPERSONAL/repos","site_admin":false,"starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/TESTPERSONAL/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/TESTPERSONAL/subscriptions","type":"User","url":"https://api.github.com/users/TESTPERSONAL","user_view_type":"public"},"comments_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/Hive-Academy/ptah-extension/commits/bce36057c6c52b8ed932be9f5ded11ed476b0e2f/comments","commit":{"author":{"date":"2026-10-05T20:52:17Z","email":"test@test.com","name":"Test"},"comment_count":0,"committer":{"date":"2026-10-05T20:52:17Z","email":"test@test.com","name":"Test"},"message":"fix: address the PR 655 CodeRabbit review findings\n\n- agent-sdk: an older run can no longer reclaim a newer run''s session\n  id in runOwners after a rekey; held subagent starts are held and\n  discarded under one payload-first parent-session id; the stream\n  callback failure handler logs visibly; the Read outline counts a\n  terminal newline correctly.\n- vscode-core: held-start discards are scoped to the parent session\n  (agentId is unique only within one session).\n- vscode-lm-tools: a duplicate in-flight session_submit id is refused\n  instead of overwriting the first call''s entry.\n- chat-streaming: an unmatched usage entry is stamped with its parent\n  session once a later message names it.\n\nImplemented on a codex CLI lane, reviewed cross-side by a code-logic\nsubagent over two revise rounds (final verdict APPROVED).\n\nCo-Authored-By: Claude Opus 5.5 <noreply@anthropic.com>","tree":{"sha":"c975e02d107275be4a9bfefbe2dc00e1a01ffacc","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/Hive-Academy/ptah-extension/git/trees/c975e02d107275be4a9bfefbe2dc00e1a01ffacc"},"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/Hive-Academy/ptah-extension/git/commits/bce36057c6c52b8ed